### 7. Digital Wallet Endpoints

#### Apple Pay

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `/v1/wallet/apple-pay/register-domain` | POST | Register and verify domain with Apple |
| `/v1/wallet/apple-pay/session` | POST | Validate merchant session with Apple servers |
| `/v1/wallet/apple-pay/charge` | POST | Decrypt and charge an Apple Pay token |

#### Google Pay

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `/v1/wallet/google-pay/charge` | POST | Decrypt and charge a Google Pay token |

Both wallets are also automatically available on the hosted checkout page when the `wallets` parameter is set:

```json
{
  "wallets": ["APPLE_PAY", "GOOGLE_PAY"]
}
```

